{"title":"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Albert starts to make a list, in increasing order, of the positive integers that have a first digit of 1. He writes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/7783215fb137d64b3e348ce4351404c5c8e8d35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 10, 11, 12, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> but by the 1,000th digit he (finally) realizes that the list would contain an infinite number of elements. Find the three-digit number formed by the last three digits he wrote (the 998th, 999th, and 1000th digits, in that order).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb460a33e48501fa9f1fca1b059f01099322dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x_1, y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad4d2d69f1db146bc3f0aa7c92eab3e6ce35b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(x_2, y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> are chosen on the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac437b09da7c98f3c56607086126fb55ef44f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\ln x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d24d4765b2ba34b600b5c0da91f9d3c497fe07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x_1 &lt; x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> trisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be20b1dbbd31212c5d1eda81c7c95eb798bc07ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC &lt; CB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> a horizontal line is drawn to cut the curve at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba0bb204ed937a5b3117b5146d206a6d6f7909cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(x_3, y_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd241834905de5246fcbb2444ed65f963fccbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da890ccfccbece41de9ef2f8dea090a5f41a3b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest prime factor of the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d789ad37258b756c76b4efa4c5371ee81c731e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\ldots , r_{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"11\" /> are distinct integers such that the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61aa06d350f214320f46afa5cef76fe9c6795eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-r_{1})(x-r_{2})\\cdots (x-r_{2006})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"18\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> nonzero coefficients.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on the circumference of a unit circle so that the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa12b63f50f8f59c47be09fd2d60b8f7b9ff8153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b827998def193fbf2d8ec73227dc09a0a27e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d0d9b28b429ef7a98b6ac8e14b6151af91ed33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, and the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81c3192e927f96cd29814267058d9daae39b810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{AC}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/983e30a3f86562e7b3c391929433e7d4e59bba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. The area of the triangular shape bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> and line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a57a55c6ae7038b60d65938db833c70e86c42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n} \\cdot \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many 10-digit positive integers have all digits either 1 or 2, and have two consecutive 1's?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de87a38aa7b2c7b68a8fb7ec6a311c219bce70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> does there exist a regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-sided polygon such that the number of diagonals is a nonzero perfect square?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa2b34b22815be18bd77e76b0880f753e226d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{3^{3^3}}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"22\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of increasing sequences of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae27509a1c37421f5082606896124c4410430072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 \\le a_2 \\le a_3 \\le \\cdots \\le a_{10} \\le 2007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf96ba96e219446aa7be5a47e66d309e1d2e7d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is even for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d8c006ddfcc323b96a35f66a1be1dc713e11e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d2e0d4016a0d15ed8e66d040c08a3960bc4bf44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${m \\choose n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"40\" height=\"53\" /> for some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0b58b81ad8d1281aaf0c31d8bf23d6e26cf24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. Compute the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 8\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nCompute the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that the fraction </p><center><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18a5b9684545b908b6b48873e88ca270d98150d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7k+100}{5k-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" /></p></center><p> is reducible.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 9\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nCompute the remainder when </p><center><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/d/26d4091db88b1937ee8cbdc4f3a3ad31eda2f726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2007 \\choose 0} + {2007 \\choose 3} + \\cdots + {2007 \\choose 2007}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"277\" height=\"53\" /></p></center><p> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 10\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an equilateral triangle. Two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acda72a653f2bdb7a89b1d073b29ea2c73244531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is 13 and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bbdaf51a8a1faae81886d50358cbaf053ae08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is 3. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9af2c3021827c9ce3706e8f430ea292389a4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CE}{EA}=\\frac{p+\\sqrt{q}}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 11\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of partitions of 2007 that have an even number of even parts can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8be4a03400384a2719b865cf815f46d4f857be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^b$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is prime. Find the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 12\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nThe sum </p><center><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a75ada4d14537951997bb6be501de00e463f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{2007} \\arctan\\left(\\frac{1}{k^2+k+1}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"190\" height=\"50\" /></p></center><p> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06ac14003f76f1fa0245005b27838e0ec16b2ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan\\left(\\frac{m}{n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a7986370c73f39e8e4cc79eaa379bac4e14eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(m,n) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. Compute the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by 100.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 13\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the arithmetic mean of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a888f45d4249c56130948206c08cdb9365f5ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;577$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> such that </p><center><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5455b740a3bd6bf8ebd43994433bb27c6513f8f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^4\\equiv 144\\pmod {577}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" />.</p></center><p> Find the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 14\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> of length 43, 13, and 48, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circle circumscribed around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> that is not on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d26a03d410fa1cc4f3af6e22ef47a7452804e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 15\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007\">Mock AIME 4 2006-2007</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017212031\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 522/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16379/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4410:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017212031 and revision id 12193. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}